  "id": "localization",
  "shortLabel": "Localization",
  "problem": "Region-proposal pipelines cannot be optimized jointly end-to-end because their two stages are separate.",
  "statements": [
   "Region-proposal pipelines cannot be optimized jointly end-to-end because their two stages are separate.",
   "Small objects (faces, far-away cars) are hard to detect in proposal-based systems because candidate boxes are low resolution and lack context.",
   "General proposal methods designed for general detection lose recall on small-sized faces and faces with complex appearance variation.",
   "Per-RoI subnetworks repeat expensive computation for every region, hurting training and testing efficiency.",
   "A fully convolutional detector with RoI pooling only after the last conv layer has considerably inferior accuracy.",
   "Deepening the RoI-wise subnetwork (as in the ResNet detection pipeline) restores accuracy but reintroduces unshared per-region cost.",
   "Bounding box regression in deep CNN detectors treats the four box bounds as independent variables optimized separately under l2 loss, contrary to the observation that they are correlated.",
   "The unnormalized l2 loss penalizes errors on large boxes more than small ones, so networks focus on larger objects and ignore smaller ones.",
   "Traditional region proposal stages are both a localization bottleneck and a computational bottleneck for real-time deployment.",
   "Most detection methods are constrained to a small set of objects because detection datasets are limited compared to classification datasets.",
   "Labeling images for detection is far more expensive than labeling for classification or tagging.",
   "YOLO makes a significant number of localization errors and has relatively low recall compared to region proposal-based methods.",
   "CNN modules sample at fixed locations and pool at fixed ratios, so they lack internal mechanisms to handle geometric transformations.",
   "All activation units in a CNN layer share the same receptive field size, which is undesirable when objects at different locations have different scales or deformation."
  ],
