   "Anchor-based one-stage detectors need huge hand-designed anchor sets (more than 40k in DSSD, more than 100k in RetinaNet).",
   "Only a tiny fraction of anchors overlap ground truth, creating a huge positive/negative imbalance that slows training.",
   "Anchor design introduces many hyperparameters and heuristic choices (sizes, aspect ratios, IoU thresholds).",
   "Horizontal RoIs in densely packed aerial scenes contain multiple instances, causing misalignment between region features and objects.",
   "Rotated anchor designs multiply the number of anchors (e.g. 3 scales x 5 aspect ratios x 6 angles = 90 anchors per location), raising computation and degrading proposal-ground-truth matching.",
