   "Trained with scratch transformers, DETR needs large-scale training data and an extreme long training schedule even on COCO.",
   "DETR performs poorly on PASCAL VOC, which has insufficient training data and fewer instances than COCO.",
   "Existing contrastive pretext tasks focus on feature discrimination rather than the spatial localization the DETR transformer performs.",
   "Popular unsupervised methods pre-train the backbone, but DETR's transformer (about 18.0M parameters) has never been pre-trained.",
   "Annotation is a time-consuming and expensive bottleneck for scaling up training data.",
   "Multi-stage pseudo-label methods train an initial detector on a small labeled set, then pseudo-label and re-train, so pseudo-label quality limits final performance.",
   "Pseudo-labeling for detection is harder than for classification because annotations contain both location and category.",
   "A high foreground-score threshold needed for precise positive pseudo labels leaves many true foreground candidates mislabeled as background.",
   "Foreground score does not reliably indicate localization accuracy, so score-filtered pseudo boxes are unsuitable for training box regression.",
   "Detection models trained on a fixed category set require additional labeled data to generalize to new visual concepts and domains.",
   "Human-annotated detection annotations are expensive to scale, and even the largest detection datasets cover no more than about 2,000 categories."
